 ## Background
-TensoRF was introduced by Anpei Chen, Zexiang Xu, Andreas Geiger, Jingyi Yu, and Hao Su in the paper "Tensorf: Tensorial Radiance Fields" presented at ECCV 2022 [S7, unofficial]. It was developed to address the computational inefficiency and large memory footprint of MLP-based NeRFs and concurrent explicit methods like Plenoxels. The method leverages tensor factorization (CP and VM) to decompose the 4D radiance field into low-rank components, enabling efficient trilinear interpolation and differentiable rendering [S1][S7, unofficial]. It has been widely used as a baseline for subsequent low-rank and tensor-based radiance field research [S1, S4].
